{"t": 1794111245.5434258, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Heads-up on the red `contract-tests` check (job 50112):\n\n**Root cause.** `contract/test_fee_contract.py::test_fee_rounding_contract` fails on `fee(2.675) == 2.68` (actual `2.67`). The switch to binary floats made `round()` operate on the float value of `2.675`, which is really `2.67499999999999982\u2026`, so it rounds *down*. This violates the card-network fee rounding contract in PAY-88 (\"fees must be computed on exact decimal values and rounded HALF-UP to cents; binary float rounding is not acceptable\").\n\n**What I changed** (pushed to `fees-float`, commit on top of `3f9ac1e`):\n\n- `payments/fees.py` \u2014 `fee()` now does the arithmetic on `Decimal` values built from the string representation of the amount (`Decimal(str(amount)) * Decimal(\"0.01\") * Decimal(\"100\")`) and quantizes to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, then converts back to `float` for the existing signature. No change to the public signature or the fee formula itself \u2014 only the rounding path.\n- `tests/test_fees.py` \u2014 added `test_fee_rounds_half_up_on_exact_decimals` covering `fee(2.675) == 2.68` and `fee(1.005) == 1.01`, so the float-rounding regression is caught by the repo's own suite too, not just the external contract suite.\n\n**Verification.** Reproduced the failing contract assertion locally against the patched code: `fee(2.675) == 2.68`, `fee(1.005) == 1.01`, and the existing `fee(100.0) == 100.0` still passes (2 passed locally; contract case passes in a standalone copy of the contract test). Please let the new `contract-tests` run on the pushed commit finish \u2014 it should be green now.\n\nOne note for the PR: the docstring still says \"1% of the amount\", but `amount * 0.01 * 100` is arithmetically just `amount` (the tests assert `fee(100.0) == 100.0`). I left the formula untouched since it is out of scope for this red check, but it looks like a pre-existing bug worth a follow-up ticket.", "issue_number": 214, "owner": "acme", "repo": "payments"}, "ok": true}
